Silent failure when adapter is null: The code silently skips metadata persistence if the adapter is not available. This could lead to data loss or inconsistent state without user feedback. Consider adding a warning toast or throwing an error when the adapter is unavailable, especially since this is a critical operation where users expect their data to be saved. For example, after the try block starts, you could check if adapter is null and handle it explicitly.
```suggestion
        if (!client) {
          toast.error('Unable to create application: no data adapter is configured');
          throw new Error('No data adapter available for metadata persistence');
        }
        await client.meta.saveItem('app', draft.name, appSchema);
```

